    ":question/id": "f56d7103-cc41-5b12-a3ac-e3e18a2f979d",
    ":question/problem": "Find $AB$, if \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.$",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\cdot 0 & 4\\cdot (-5) \\\\ (-8)\\cdot 0 & (-8)\\cdot (-5) \\\\ 3\\cdot 0 & 3\\cdot (-5)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -20 \\\\ 0 & 40 \\\\ 0 & -15\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
